1
00:01:54,448 --> 00:01:57,201
No, no, no. Don't feed the dog, darling.

2
00:02:04,541 --> 00:02:06,009
Thanks, babe.

3
00:02:06,543 --> 00:02:08,716
- You slept late.
- Yeah, I need to go.

4
00:02:08,795 --> 00:02:10,138
What you got going today?

5
00:02:10,213 --> 00:02:13,467
I've got to finish up some curtains
for Saturday,

6
00:02:13,550 --> 00:02:15,928
and Nat and Cam are coming over.

7
00:02:16,011 --> 00:02:17,479
- With the kids?
- Yeah.

8
00:02:17,554 --> 00:02:19,431
Cammie said she just needed
to get out of the house.

9
00:02:19,514 --> 00:02:21,608
Tell Nat to take it easy on her.

10
00:02:21,683 --> 00:02:23,481
Cam can hold her own.

11
00:02:23,560 --> 00:02:26,313
We need to send in the deposit
for the beach condo.

12
00:02:26,396 --> 00:02:27,898
I love you.

13
00:02:32,027 --> 00:02:35,031
- Just write the check, babe, okay?
- Okay. Bye.

14
00:02:41,244 --> 00:02:43,087
No more food.

15
00:02:44,081 --> 00:02:45,333
You, eat.

16
00:03:24,955 --> 00:03:27,208
Yeah, let's keep going with that bit.

17
00:03:27,290 --> 00:03:28,792
It'll go another 10 feet.

18
00:03:29,668 --> 00:03:31,466
We won't get the gravel pack down today.

19
00:03:31,545 --> 00:03:32,797
Why not?

20
00:03:34,339 --> 00:03:35,556
Clouds.

21
00:03:36,800 --> 00:03:38,643
We're gonna have to call it.

22
00:03:38,760 --> 00:03:40,979
Happy hour starts at 5:00, Dewart.

23
00:03:41,972 --> 00:03:43,724
Not if it's raining.

24
00:03:46,268 --> 00:03:47,736
- Ready?
- Yeah.

25
00:03:50,480 --> 00:03:52,574
They were just drinking and laughing

26
00:03:52,649 --> 00:03:56,244
And, oh, my God,
it was like I was being in a museum

27
00:03:56,319 --> 00:04:00,165
and I saw the progress from apes to men.

28
00:04:00,824 --> 00:04:03,703
I saw it. I saw the future.

29
00:04:04,911 --> 00:04:08,506
Dewart, that was him,
that was going to be him in 20 years.

30
00:04:10,333 --> 00:04:12,256
Let me tell you, you laugh.

31
00:04:12,669 --> 00:04:17,175
You laugh. But this little one in your arms is
gonna be shuffling in a bar just like them.

32
00:04:17,841 --> 00:04:20,139
- Yep.
- No.

33
00:04:20,260 --> 00:04:21,887
Don't listen to her.

34
00:04:21,970 --> 00:04:23,472
- Hannah!
- What?

35
00:04:29,770 --> 00:04:31,568
- You guys okay?
- Yeah.

36
00:04:34,065 --> 00:04:35,692
No. Don't touch.

37
00:04:36,777 --> 00:04:38,324
You understand?

38
00:04:43,033 --> 00:04:44,125
Okay. Come here.

39
00:04:48,830 --> 00:04:50,047
Go play.

40
00:05:14,898 --> 00:05:17,321
Hey, DJ. Bring the girls inside.

41
00:05:31,915 --> 00:05:33,041
What?

42
00:05:34,125 --> 00:05:37,299
- It's not my fault. I told you.
- Yeah, all right.

43
00:05:38,547 --> 00:05:41,266
All right, I'm calling it. Shut it down.

44
00:05:45,804 --> 00:05:48,523
- Bye, guys. Thank you for coming.
- I'll call you about the Lions Club supper.

45
00:05:48,598 --> 00:05:49,941
- Okay. Love you.
- Bye, Sam.

46
00:05:50,016 --> 00:05:51,438
BYE, Cam!

47
00:06:14,916 --> 00:06:16,793
Can you sign

48
00:06:18,420 --> 00:06:23,142
S-T-O-R-M?

49
00:06:29,014 --> 00:06:30,641
Storm.

50
00:07:00,003 --> 00:07:01,630
I gotta get home.

51
00:07:13,600 --> 00:07:16,399
Nat and me been looking into a threesome.

52
00:07:22,192 --> 00:07:24,615
We've been chatting with this girl online
from Canton.

53
00:07:25,195 --> 00:07:26,913
Yeah. Big old girl.

54
00:07:30,867 --> 00:07:32,119
What's big?

55
00:07:32,202 --> 00:07:34,671
She's about 250, 275.

56
00:07:34,913 --> 00:07:36,756
She can't be no taller than five foot.

57
00:07:42,379 --> 00:07:43,722
Shit, man.

58
00:07:47,008 --> 00:07:49,852
I don't see me and Sam
getting into something like that.

59
00:07:49,928 --> 00:07:52,056
No. I don't guess you would.

60
00:07:56,393 --> 00:07:58,566
You got a good life, Curtis.

61
00:07:58,895 --> 00:08:00,317
I'm serious.

62
00:08:01,898 --> 00:08:05,573
I think that's the best compliment
you can give a man,

63
00:08:05,652 --> 00:08:09,122
take a look at his life
and say, "That's good.

64
00:08:10,532 --> 00:08:12,079
"That guy's doing something right."

65
00:08:14,619 --> 00:08:16,747
Well, it ain't always so easy.

66
00:08:17,080 --> 00:08:18,753
Hell, I know that.

67
00:08:22,127 --> 00:08:24,004
Shit. I gotta go.

68
00:08:30,677 --> 00:08:32,054
Good night.

69
00:09:24,939 --> 00:09:26,282
Hey, baby.

70
00:09:31,654 --> 00:09:33,702
She do all right today?

71
00:09:35,492 --> 00:09:36,960
She was fine.

72
00:09:38,661 --> 00:09:41,084
She's still not playing
with the others, though.

73
00:09:41,164 --> 00:09:42,791
She can't connect.

74
00:09:44,334 --> 00:09:46,632
Honey, you gotta clean up that trash pile
in the back.

75
00:09:47,128 --> 00:09:50,052
She fished out <i>a</i>
board that had nails on it.

76
00:09:52,342 --> 00:09:54,470
I'll get to it this weekend.

77
00:10:00,683 --> 00:10:03,857
I still take off my boots,
so I won't wake her up.

78
00:10:06,439 --> 00:10:08,032
I still whisper.

79
00:11:50,752 --> 00:11:51,799
Curtis?

80
00:11:51,961 --> 00:11:54,635
- What?
- Did you hear me?

81
00:11:54,714 --> 00:11:58,844
You got to be home, showered,
ready to walk out the door by 6:00 tonight.

82
00:11:59,093 --> 00:12:00,515
What's wrong?

83
00:12:00,595 --> 00:12:05,021
Nothing. I just want her to eat her breakfast
and stop playing with the damn dog.

84
00:12:05,099 --> 00:12:06,567
She's fine down there.
She had toast already.

85
00:12:06,643 --> 00:12:07,860
- All right.
- What?

86
00:12:07,936 --> 00:12:09,438
Hannah. Come here. Hannah.

87
00:12:09,520 --> 00:12:11,022
- Curtis?
- What?

88
00:12:16,903 --> 00:12:18,155
I'm late.

89
00:12:18,780 --> 00:12:21,329
- You didn't eat anything.
- It's okay.

90
00:12:26,788 --> 00:12:29,337
I didn't say you had control
over the weather, Russell.

91
00:12:29,415 --> 00:12:34,467
What I did say was that the top shelf
has got to be cleared by the 15th.

92
00:12:34,545 --> 00:12:36,798
That's non-negotiable.

93
00:12:38,132 --> 00:12:39,349
Curtis?

94
00:12:39,717 --> 00:12:42,596
Curtis? Where we at on that East 82nd site?

95
00:12:42,679 --> 00:12:46,934
Yesterday slowed us down.
We couldn't get the second pilot hole drilled.

96
00:12:47,475 --> 00:12:50,069
It rained for two hours yesterday.

97
00:12:50,144 --> 00:12:54,365
Two hours,
and our entire schedule went in the toilet?

98
00:12:54,440 --> 00:12:56,863
We lose the permit
if you're not out of there, end of day.

99
00:12:57,193 --> 00:12:59,446
- Yes, sir.
- End of day, Curtis.

100
00:13:00,196 --> 00:13:04,076
All right. Valerie tells me
that the father-son pancake cook-off...

101
00:13:06,160 --> 00:13:08,959
Hey, I gotta make a stop
before we head out there.

102
00:13:09,038 --> 00:13:11,757
- Think we got time?
- Yeah, there's time.

103
00:13:13,459 --> 00:13:14,585
Shit.

104
00:13:33,563 --> 00:13:35,065
Son of a bitch.

105
00:13:35,606 --> 00:13:37,233
- We stripped that bit.
- Yeah.

106
00:13:38,026 --> 00:13:40,620
Well, bring it up. We gotta reset it.

107
00:14:22,278 --> 00:14:23,495
Curtis!

108
00:14:37,919 --> 00:14:41,389
- You ever see birds fly like that?
- What?

109
00:14:55,728 --> 00:14:56,980
Damn it.

110
00:14:58,648 --> 00:14:59,865
Damn it.

111
00:15:01,776 --> 00:15:03,574
Come on, we gotta go.

112
00:15:04,237 --> 00:15:05,580
Jesus.

113
00:15:06,948 --> 00:15:09,326
Honey, I can really use a shower.

114
00:15:15,623 --> 00:15:16,670
Hi.

115
00:15:19,168 --> 00:15:21,887
So if you continue with
the basic vocabulary,

116
00:15:21,963 --> 00:15:25,058
this will allow you to communicate
with your children better.

117
00:15:25,883 --> 00:15:27,885
Between the ages of four and seven,

118
00:15:28,678 --> 00:15:30,271
the focus is more on the sign.

119
00:15:30,805 --> 00:15:33,558
And then later,
we'll begin adding the alphabet

120
00:15:33,641 --> 00:15:35,769
as more of a support system.

121
00:15:36,644 --> 00:15:41,275
Now, in ASL, the male sign is
signed at the forehead area.

122
00:15:41,357 --> 00:15:44,531
For example, "father,"
is signed up here like this.

123
00:15:45,027 --> 00:15:46,700
Father. Very good.

124
00:16:02,378 --> 00:16:04,597
- You're not sorry.
- I am sorry.

125
00:16:06,257 --> 00:16:08,885
Well, you stink. You smell really bad.

126
00:16:15,850 --> 00:16:17,648
I think I smell good.

127
00:16:24,525 --> 00:16:26,118
Do I smell good?

128
00:16:29,238 --> 00:16:32,663
See? Maybe I should marry her instead.

129
00:16:32,950 --> 00:16:34,327
Stop.

130
00:16:45,671 --> 00:16:46,923
Man.

131
00:16:58,768 --> 00:16:59,769
You okay?

132
00:17:16,369 --> 00:17:17,586
Shit!

133
00:17:36,264 --> 00:17:37,436
You okay?

134
00:17:40,309 --> 00:17:41,731
You're okay.

135
00:17:44,981 --> 00:17:46,324
It's okay.

136
00:17:54,532 --> 00:17:55,624
No!

137
00:17:55,700 --> 00:17:56,917
Hannah!

138
00:18:00,246 --> 00:18:02,544
Hannah!

139
00:18:07,336 --> 00:18:09,759
Hannah!

140
00:18:17,013 --> 00:18:20,108
Here, honey. Put on your shoes.

141
00:18:20,182 --> 00:18:21,729
- Good, you're up.
- Yeah.

142
00:18:23,185 --> 00:18:24,277
Honey, you're soaked.

143
00:18:27,273 --> 00:18:28,365
I've felt better.

144
00:18:30,693 --> 00:18:32,115
I guess we can stay home if we need to.

145
00:18:33,529 --> 00:18:34,655
Where you going?

146
00:18:34,739 --> 00:18:36,707
It's Saturday.
I was going to take Hannah to my booth.

147
00:18:36,782 --> 00:18:38,159
Yeah.

148
00:18:39,994 --> 00:18:42,122
You look really sick, honey.

149
00:18:42,913 --> 00:18:45,917
I'm all right.
It's just a cold or something.

150
00:18:46,500 --> 00:18:48,298
Let me get you some Advil.

151
00:18:48,377 --> 00:18:50,721
No. Don't worry about it.
Just go. I'll be fine.

152
00:18:50,963 --> 00:18:52,340
You sure?

153
00:18:52,757 --> 00:18:54,304
Better already.

154
00:18:56,218 --> 00:18:59,563
Okay. I got my phone if you need anything.

155
00:18:59,930 --> 00:19:01,557
Don't forget, Sunday
lunch is here tomorrow.

156
00:19:02,725 --> 00:19:04,147
If you're sick, we should cancel.

157
00:19:05,061 --> 00:19:06,153
I'll be all right.

158
00:19:08,105 --> 00:19:09,152
Okay, we'll talk later.

159
00:19:11,567 --> 00:19:13,240
Come on. Let's go.

160
00:19:14,445 --> 00:19:16,447
- You sure?
- Honey, please.

161
00:20:26,058 --> 00:20:27,480
How much you asking for this pillow?

162
00:20:28,644 --> 00:20:30,738
This pillow is $15.

163
00:20:30,813 --> 00:20:32,486
That's more than I want to spend.

164
00:20:32,815 --> 00:20:35,113
This is all hand stitched.
It takes a really long time.

165
00:20:35,192 --> 00:20:36,489
That's why I charge that.

166
00:20:37,111 --> 00:20:39,205
I'll give you $7 for it.

167
00:20:39,864 --> 00:20:40,990
I can't go that low.

168
00:20:41,490 --> 00:20:43,333
Well, that's my offer.

169
00:20:48,664 --> 00:20:50,166
How about 10?

170
00:20:52,626 --> 00:20:55,175
I'll give you $8, but it's in change.

171
00:20:57,506 --> 00:21:00,885
That's fine.
Lucky for you she likes to count change.

172
00:21:02,052 --> 00:21:03,144
Red.

173
00:21:04,972 --> 00:21:06,189
Come on.

174
00:21:06,682 --> 00:21:08,355
Get in. Good boy.

175
00:21:16,150 --> 00:21:18,278
I'm sorry about this, buddy.

176
00:21:19,528 --> 00:21:22,748
We just gotta work it like this
for a while, okay?

177
00:24:05,945 --> 00:24:08,164
<i>While rescue workers made several
attempts to reach the family,</i>

178
00:24:08,238 --> 00:24:11,117
- Walter Jacobs' <i>wife</i> and brother-in-law died.
- That's what I don't understand.

179
00:24:11,450 --> 00:24:15,375
If he didn't do anything,
why did you put him out back?

180
00:24:18,374 --> 00:24:19,466
What?

181
00:24:20,417 --> 00:24:21,509
Did you hear me?

182
00:24:21,585 --> 00:24:25,840
I said if he didn't do anything,
why did you have to put him outside?

183
00:24:26,507 --> 00:24:29,431
I just wanted him to be
outside for a while.

184
00:24:30,511 --> 00:24:32,605
He's your dog.
He's always been an inside dog.

185
00:24:32,680 --> 00:24:34,398
He's my dog, that's why he's outside.

186
00:24:38,727 --> 00:24:39,853
Look,

187
00:24:41,021 --> 00:24:46,243
right now with Hannah and everything,
I just think it'd be better.

188
00:24:47,027 --> 00:24:49,121
- Hannah loves Red.
- Hold on.

189
00:24:50,406 --> 00:24:53,501
<i>The gas cloud spread across
their six-acre property.</i>

190
00:24:53,575 --> 00:24:56,044
<i>The only way off their land
was across the train tracks,</i>

191
00:24:56,412 --> 00:24:58,255
<i>which were blocked by wreckage.</i>

192
00:24:58,330 --> 00:25:00,799
<i>I tried using some wet rags
and some towels to breathe through,</i>

193
00:25:02,126 --> 00:25:03,878
<i>but that just seemed
to make it worse.</i>

194
00:25:04,336 --> 00:25:07,556
<i>While rescue workers made several
attempts to reach the family,</i>

195
00:25:07,631 --> 00:25:11,181
<i>Walter Jacobs' wife and
brother-in-law died in the home.</i>

196
00:25:11,510 --> 00:25:16,858
<i>Jacobs survived despite enduring 11
hours of exposure to the gas cloud...</i>

197
00:25:16,932 --> 00:25:18,149
You hearing this?

198
00:25:19,268 --> 00:25:20,611
It's awful.

199
00:25:21,729 --> 00:25:23,197
Eleven hours.

200
00:25:25,566 --> 00:25:26,943
No way out.

201
00:25:51,717 --> 00:25:52,934
Hannah.

202
00:26:12,071 --> 00:26:13,163
Hey!

203
00:26:14,573 --> 00:26:15,825
Hey!

204
00:26:18,827 --> 00:26:20,704
Hey! Hey!

205
00:27:23,642 --> 00:27:25,189
- Babe?
- Yeah?

206
00:27:25,269 --> 00:27:28,694
You got the number for Dr. Shannan?

207
00:27:28,772 --> 00:27:30,490
You're still not feeling good?

208
00:27:30,566 --> 00:27:32,785
Yeah, we got the number?

209
00:27:32,860 --> 00:27:34,828
Yeah, baby, but he'll be closed today.

210
00:27:35,571 --> 00:27:37,198
Right. Yeah, I'll call tomorrow.

211
00:27:37,531 --> 00:27:38,657
Honey, if you're not feeling good,

212
00:27:38,740 --> 00:27:41,084
- we got to take you...
- No. Stop!

213
00:27:44,204 --> 00:27:45,421
Okay.

214
00:27:46,123 --> 00:27:48,342
Do you want me to cancel lunch today?

215
00:27:48,417 --> 00:27:49,509
Shit.

216
00:27:49,960 --> 00:27:51,758
- What is that?
- I'm sorry.

217
00:27:52,296 --> 00:27:54,344
I'm sorry. I just...

218
00:27:56,383 --> 00:27:59,887
I got a sore throat.
I'm sorry I'm taking it out on you.

219
00:28:01,096 --> 00:28:03,019
I was gonna leave Hannah with you
so I could go to church,

220
00:28:03,098 --> 00:28:04,600
but I'm not gonna with you like this.

221
00:28:04,766 --> 00:28:05,858
It's fine. I'll be fine.

222
00:28:05,934 --> 00:28:08,278
- No. She needs breakfast.
- I got it.

223
00:28:08,353 --> 00:28:11,653
I'm sorry that you feel bad,
but you need to drop the attitude.

224
00:28:13,775 --> 00:28:15,527
Come on. Just go.

225
00:28:17,446 --> 00:28:20,245
- What's wrong with you?
- I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

226
00:28:20,324 --> 00:28:21,576
Just go.

227
00:28:25,954 --> 00:28:28,924
Hannah's in the den.
We have cereal for her.

228
00:28:57,903 --> 00:29:01,874
We're going out.

229
00:29:03,367 --> 00:29:06,246
We're going out. Okay?

230
00:29:06,328 --> 00:29:08,672
It's okay. It's okay.

231
00:29:26,056 --> 00:29:27,524
You stay put, okay?

232
00:30:34,916 --> 00:30:36,543
Let's just start.

233
00:30:37,252 --> 00:30:39,880
Let's all join hands for the blessing.

234
00:30:50,766 --> 00:30:53,519
- Where the hell have you been?
- I know. I'm sorry. I had to run an errand.

235
00:30:53,602 --> 00:30:54,819
- You're really late.
- I know.

236
00:30:54,936 --> 00:30:57,564
You didn't even bring your cell phone.

237
00:31:07,783 --> 00:31:09,205
Missed you at church this morning, Curtis.

238
00:31:09,910 --> 00:31:11,253
Dad.

239
00:31:11,328 --> 00:31:14,548
He knows what to do
if he wants me to stop asking.

240
00:31:15,999 --> 00:31:17,876
Was it a good service?

241
00:31:18,585 --> 00:31:20,587
It was. It was good work.

242
00:31:26,134 --> 00:31:28,728
I'm thinking about cleaning up
that storm shelter out back.

243
00:33:08,737 --> 00:33:09,909
Curtis?

244
00:33:14,910 --> 00:33:17,538
- Curtis, how you doing, bud?
- Hey, Doc.

245
00:33:17,621 --> 00:33:19,464
- How's my girl?
- She's good.

246
00:33:19,539 --> 00:33:21,462
That's good to hear.
Tilt your head back for me.

247
00:33:21,541 --> 00:33:23,509
I don't have a cold.

248
00:33:23,585 --> 00:33:27,306
- Did she get that down wrong?
- No, I just told her that.

249
00:33:28,465 --> 00:33:30,342
So what's the problem?

250
00:33:31,968 --> 00:33:33,720
I've been having...

251
00:33:34,596 --> 00:33:36,598
I've been having some trouble sleeping.

252
00:33:36,681 --> 00:33:39,059
I was hoping
you could give me something for it.

253
00:33:39,142 --> 00:33:41,395
How long's this been going on?

254
00:33:41,728 --> 00:33:43,401
About four nights now.

255
00:33:43,480 --> 00:33:45,153
You're not sleeping at all?

256
00:33:45,232 --> 00:33:47,451
Well, some, but real restless.

257
00:33:48,860 --> 00:33:52,831
Well, I think four nights
is a little too soon to tell.

258
00:33:52,906 --> 00:33:56,536
My advice would be to not eat
or drink anything after 8:00 at night.

259
00:33:56,618 --> 00:34:00,794
Cut back on any alcoholic drinks,
tobacco, caffeine.

260
00:34:01,706 --> 00:34:03,674
Get some daily exercise.

261
00:34:04,292 --> 00:34:05,965
Well, I think...

262
00:34:07,796 --> 00:34:11,517
- I think I might need to try some medication.
- Why do you say that?

263
00:34:14,177 --> 00:34:18,933
The reason I've been having trouble
sleeping is these dreams I've been having.

264
00:34:19,516 --> 00:34:24,693
I didn't think it was anything at first,
but then the other day I woke up

265
00:34:27,816 --> 00:34:29,568
and the bed was wet.

266
00:34:30,151 --> 00:34:32,995
- You urinated in your bed?
- Yeah.

267
00:34:34,948 --> 00:34:37,827
Couple days before that,
I had a dream that my dog attacked me

268
00:34:37,909 --> 00:34:41,334
and it took all day
for the pain in my arm to go away.

269
00:34:47,752 --> 00:34:48,969
You been out to see your mother lately?

270
00:34:51,172 --> 00:34:53,425
It's been about a month.

271
00:34:53,508 --> 00:34:54,760
Okay.

272
00:35:04,603 --> 00:35:08,653
Okay. This is a prescription
for a pretty mild sedative.

273
00:35:08,732 --> 00:35:09,824
It's non-habit forming,

274
00:35:09,899 --> 00:35:12,402
but I'm only giving you enough
for a few days anyway.

275
00:35:12,485 --> 00:35:15,409
Take it and see if it helps.
In the meantime,

276
00:35:15,488 --> 00:35:19,038
this is the number of a good friend of mine
in Columbus. He's a psychiatrist.

277
00:35:19,868 --> 00:35:22,587
It's a drive, but he's the best I know.

278
00:35:25,040 --> 00:35:26,166
Okay.

279
00:35:26,541 --> 00:35:30,512
I'll give him a call
and let him know you'll be down to see him.

280
00:35:30,879 --> 00:35:32,222
All right.

281
00:35:47,896 --> 00:35:50,490
- Hey, Dewart.
- What you say, Curtis?

282
00:35:50,565 --> 00:35:51,862
Not much.

283
00:35:52,734 --> 00:35:54,953
They want us
to get a pilot hole drilled by lunch.

284
00:35:55,028 --> 00:35:56,826
I figure worse comes to worse,
we can eat on the rig.

285
00:35:56,905 --> 00:35:58,828
Yeah, we'll get it done. Weekend all right?

286
00:35:58,907 --> 00:36:00,250
Yeah. Same old shit.

287
00:36:01,910 --> 00:36:06,666
No. No, I need the name of the specialist
whose diagnosis you'll accept.

288
00:36:09,501 --> 00:36:11,674
No. Look it, I've told you this twice.
Please.

289
00:36:11,753 --> 00:36:14,848
Just get me the name
and/or the approval code.

290
00:36:16,549 --> 00:36:17,766
Okay.

291
00:36:21,262 --> 00:36:23,765
All right. And the phone? All right.

292
00:36:25,725 --> 00:36:27,898
Great. Well, thank you very much.

293
00:36:28,436 --> 00:36:31,030
All right, this is the name
and the phone number of the specialist

294
00:36:31,106 --> 00:36:33,029
who the insurance company approves of.

295
00:36:33,108 --> 00:36:34,985
Just call and make an appointment.

296
00:36:35,068 --> 00:36:37,036
Now if this doctor signs off,

297
00:36:37,112 --> 00:36:39,786
you should have the implant procedure
fully covered.

298
00:36:40,490 --> 00:36:42,413
I'm sorry it took so long.

299
00:36:44,869 --> 00:36:47,042
Can I give you a hug?

300
00:36:47,122 --> 00:36:48,874
It's fine. It's fine.

301
00:36:49,666 --> 00:36:53,296
You know, your husband's company actually
has very good insurance when it kicks in.

302
00:36:53,378 --> 00:36:57,133
Not a lot of jobs offer policies half
<i>as</i> good. You're very lucky.

303
00:37:04,931 --> 00:37:07,650
That's okay.
We have your insurance on file.

304
00:37:07,726 --> 00:37:10,525
- That'll be $47.64.
- What's the co-pay?

305
00:37:11,229 --> 00:37:12,401
That is your co-pay.

306
00:37:28,538 --> 00:37:29,630
Hey.

307
00:37:41,050 --> 00:37:42,427
I love you.

308
00:37:43,344 --> 00:37:44,937
I love you too.

309
00:37:50,477 --> 00:37:52,104
I have good news.

310
00:37:57,275 --> 00:37:59,573
Green? How about a red?

311
00:38:08,369 --> 00:38:12,374
It was like talking to a
sane person for once.

312
00:38:15,043 --> 00:38:17,546
She made one phone call. That's it.

313
00:38:18,797 --> 00:38:21,721
I've been trying that 800 number
for weeks. You.

314
00:38:22,884 --> 00:38:24,932
It's great. It's great.

315
00:38:27,055 --> 00:38:28,432
Hey, Hannah.

316
00:38:35,188 --> 00:38:38,738
Are you excited?
We're gonna get you some help.

317
00:38:38,858 --> 00:38:41,532
How do you say, sign, "excited"?

318
00:38:41,611 --> 00:38:42,954
Like this.

319
00:38:44,364 --> 00:38:46,412
Excited? Yeah?

320
00:38:50,036 --> 00:38:52,630
All right. What've we got here?

321
00:38:52,747 --> 00:38:54,465
I got to do you.

322
00:38:55,917 --> 00:38:57,715
Honey, look at this one.

323
00:38:58,628 --> 00:39:03,099
It's a 2-1, and it sits
directly on the beach.

324
00:39:04,425 --> 00:39:07,895
Wouldn't that be great? We wouldn't have
to worry about Hannah crossing traffic.

325
00:39:07,971 --> 00:39:10,190
- What's the rent?
- $899 a week.

326
00:39:12,851 --> 00:39:14,398
That sounds real nice.

327
00:40:18,917 --> 00:40:20,464
You sleep well?

328
00:40:20,877 --> 00:40:22,299
Yeah. I did.

329
00:40:23,004 --> 00:40:25,507
You look like you're feeling better.

330
00:40:29,969 --> 00:40:32,267
You want me to come up there
and do it for you?

331
00:40:32,347 --> 00:40:33,519
Jesus.

332
00:40:33,932 --> 00:40:36,606
Hey, how much food you think you'd need
to live on for a week?

333
00:40:36,684 --> 00:40:39,107
- What do you mean?
- I mean to stay alive.

334
00:40:39,187 --> 00:40:41,440
What do you think you'd need?

335
00:40:41,522 --> 00:40:44,116
- Not a lot.
- Yeah? You think?

336
00:40:44,192 --> 00:40:45,444
I don't know.

337
00:40:45,526 --> 00:40:50,123
You hear about people living for days
all the time off bark and melted snow.

338
00:40:52,200 --> 00:40:54,202
I've never heard of that.

339
00:40:54,702 --> 00:40:55,999
Shit, I don't know. You asked the question.

340
00:40:57,538 --> 00:40:59,040
It's on there.

341
00:40:59,165 --> 00:41:00,792
It's on. Come on.

342
00:41:09,550 --> 00:41:10,893
Damn it.

343
00:41:11,886 --> 00:41:13,433
What?

344
00:41:13,846 --> 00:41:15,723
It sounds like thunder.

345
00:41:16,099 --> 00:41:17,601
What sounds like thunder?

346
00:41:23,648 --> 00:41:25,195
What's the matter with you, Curtis?

347
00:41:32,407 --> 00:41:33,704
Curtis?

348
00:41:43,710 --> 00:41:46,133
Where you going? Curtis, where you going?

349
00:43:27,939 --> 00:43:29,612
- Curtis.
- Hey, Mom.

350
00:43:45,039 --> 00:43:46,586
- Come in.
- Sure.

351
00:43:56,050 --> 00:43:58,052
I'm gonna get some water.

352
00:44:15,069 --> 00:44:16,571
You want some?

353
00:44:17,822 --> 00:44:18,869
No.

354
00:44:23,369 --> 00:44:24,996
Isn't she lovely?

355
00:44:34,422 --> 00:44:36,516
- Mom?
- Yes?

356
00:44:36,591 --> 00:44:38,764
I need to ask you something.

357
00:44:40,720 --> 00:44:43,849
Do you remember what year
we brought you up here?

358
00:44:43,931 --> 00:44:45,683
To the first place.

359
00:44:50,438 --> 00:44:51,781
It was '86.

360
00:44:53,566 --> 00:44:57,412
Yes. Because Kyle was going to be a senior.

361
00:44:59,530 --> 00:45:01,532
- I was 10.
- Yes.

362
00:45:03,951 --> 00:45:09,333
Can you remember what happened
before you got diagnosed?

363
00:45:09,415 --> 00:45:11,509
- What do you mean?
- I mean...

364
00:45:12,960 --> 00:45:15,713
I just want to know how it all started.

365
00:45:15,796 --> 00:45:17,798
Before you had to leave.

366
00:45:18,382 --> 00:45:20,134
I don't know.

367
00:45:29,352 --> 00:45:32,606
I remember it was a real stressful time.

368
00:45:36,442 --> 00:45:39,321
Your father was gone a lot,

369
00:45:40,112 --> 00:45:42,831
and I couldn't handle things on my own.

370
00:45:45,993 --> 00:45:47,961
Did you ever have any

371
00:45:49,872 --> 00:45:51,249
dreams?

372
00:45:51,332 --> 00:45:53,255
Like, bad dreams?

373
00:45:55,753 --> 00:45:58,347
No. Nothing like that.

374
00:46:05,346 --> 00:46:07,064
There was always...

375
00:46:11,018 --> 00:46:13,567
There was always a panic

376
00:46:14,689 --> 00:46:17,112
that took hold of me.

377
00:46:22,280 --> 00:46:25,659
I thought people were watching me
and listening to me.

378
00:46:26,075 --> 00:46:28,874
It's all right. It's fine.

379
00:46:36,460 --> 00:46:37,928
Are you okay?

380
00:46:39,880 --> 00:46:41,006
Yeah.

381
00:46:42,758 --> 00:46:44,305
Yeah. I'm fine.

382
00:46:51,767 --> 00:46:54,737
May I have the number
for Dr. George Shannan?

383
00:46:56,689 --> 00:46:57,906
Thanks.

384
00:47:01,444 --> 00:47:03,663
Hi, is Dr. Shannan there?

385
00:47:05,281 --> 00:47:08,876
May I speak with him?
This is Curtis LaForche.

386
00:47:12,204 --> 00:47:13,751
Hey, Doc.

387
00:47:15,833 --> 00:47:19,178
Yeah, sorry... Sorry to call you at home.

388
00:47:19,253 --> 00:47:23,850
I just... I don't think I can make it
to Columbus to see that psychiatrist.

389
00:47:24,508 --> 00:47:27,307
Yeah, it's just too far.

390
00:47:28,179 --> 00:47:31,353
Is there somewhere local
you could send me?

391
00:47:50,951 --> 00:47:51,998
Hey.

392
00:47:52,703 --> 00:47:53,955
Hey.

393
00:47:54,997 --> 00:47:56,795
Sorry I woke you up.

394
00:47:58,209 --> 00:47:59,552
It's okay.

395
00:48:01,754 --> 00:48:03,301
Where you been?

396
00:48:03,839 --> 00:48:05,512
I went to see Mom.

397
00:48:07,968 --> 00:48:09,345
Is she okay?

398
00:48:11,472 --> 00:48:14,191
Yeah. I just wanted to check up on her.

399
00:48:15,101 --> 00:48:17,195
You should've told me,
we would have gone with you.

400
00:48:17,269 --> 00:48:18,862
No, that's okay.

401
00:48:24,026 --> 00:48:25,448
Come to bed.

402
00:48:27,154 --> 00:48:28,747
I will in a bit.

403
00:49:07,778 --> 00:49:09,906
Well, you've kept up with the payments
on the house.

404
00:49:10,030 --> 00:49:11,828
We've been good about that.

405
00:49:11,907 --> 00:49:16,003
I gotta tell you, Curtis, banks aren't
loaning money the way they used to.

406
00:49:16,078 --> 00:49:19,457
We've got you a loan today,
but the interest rates are variable.

407
00:49:19,540 --> 00:49:20,962
We have to tie it to your house.

408
00:49:21,041 --> 00:49:22,418
That's fine.

409
00:49:24,628 --> 00:49:26,471
Curtis, I've known you a long time.

410
00:49:26,547 --> 00:49:29,642
Financed your house for you, two vehicles.

411
00:49:29,717 --> 00:49:33,017
I'm telling you,
this is a risky loan you're taking.

412
00:49:34,722 --> 00:49:36,645
I need the money, John.

413
00:49:39,101 --> 00:49:40,227
Okay.

414
00:49:51,030 --> 00:49:53,249
- Hey.
- Hey.

415
00:49:54,450 --> 00:49:56,578
Sorry I left you yesterday.

416
00:49:57,995 --> 00:50:00,919
- Jim came by. I covered for you.
- Thanks.

417
00:50:02,666 --> 00:50:05,715
- I need your help with the depth charts.
- Sure.

418
00:50:15,596 --> 00:50:20,102
Fucking Nat put me in charge of frying
oysters for that Lions Club supper.

419
00:50:21,727 --> 00:50:23,855
You need another burner?

420
00:50:23,938 --> 00:50:26,942
Yeah, if you still got
yours, I could use it.

421
00:50:33,948 --> 00:50:36,872
Hey, you think you could help me
with something?

422
00:50:36,951 --> 00:50:38,123
What do you need?

423
00:50:38,202 --> 00:50:41,797
I'm gonna build out the tornado shelter
in my backyard. I could use some help.

424
00:50:42,122 --> 00:50:44,420
The hell you wanna do that for?

425
00:50:45,793 --> 00:50:47,670
Just needs to be done.

426
00:50:51,131 --> 00:50:52,348
What do you need?

427
00:50:52,716 --> 00:50:56,846
I figure I'll do it on a Saturday,
borrow some equipment from work.

428
00:50:58,305 --> 00:51:01,559
- You sure about that?
- Yeah, I just need a backhoe, a hauler.

429
00:51:01,642 --> 00:51:03,360
I'll rent the rest.

430
00:51:08,566 --> 00:51:11,490
- Yeah. Whatever. I'll help.
- Thanks.

431
00:51:20,536 --> 00:51:23,164
- You all right, man?
- What do you mean?

432
00:51:26,792 --> 00:51:29,090
I just don't wanna see you fuck up.

433
00:51:33,632 --> 00:51:34,849
I'm not.

434
00:51:49,315 --> 00:51:50,362
Come in.

435
00:51:53,277 --> 00:51:54,620
- Hi.
- Hello.

436
00:51:55,613 --> 00:51:58,207
- Have a seat. I'm Kendra.
- Curtis.

437
00:51:58,365 --> 00:51:59,366
Okay.

438
00:52:00,993 --> 00:52:03,462
I'm gonna start
by asking you some questions.

439
00:52:03,537 --> 00:52:07,041
Okay. I already answered
all the questions on the form.

440
00:52:07,374 --> 00:52:11,550
Yeah, I know. I looked at them,
but I need to get a profile started on you.

441
00:52:11,629 --> 00:52:13,552
Right. Well...

442
00:52:16,800 --> 00:52:21,351
Out of the five possible symptoms
needed to be diagnosed with schizophrenia,

443
00:52:21,764 --> 00:52:24,984
delusions, hallucinations,
disorganized speech,

444
00:52:25,059 --> 00:52:28,689
disorganized behavior
and the negative symptoms,

445
00:52:30,397 --> 00:52:32,024
I've had two.

446
00:52:33,400 --> 00:52:35,528
Delusions and hallucinations.

447
00:52:36,153 --> 00:52:40,579
So, I took this quiz in
the back of the book.

448
00:52:40,658 --> 00:52:45,004
I scored a five out of a possible 20.

449
00:52:45,454 --> 00:52:48,082
Schizophrenia starts at 12. So...

450
00:52:50,584 --> 00:52:53,838
They say it might be
a brief psychotic disorder.

451
00:52:56,382 --> 00:52:59,101
Yeah. Whatever it is,
I need to know what to do

452
00:53:00,135 --> 00:53:03,309
or what to get on
to get this thing under control.

453
00:53:06,892 --> 00:53:08,815
Look. I'm a counselor.

454
00:53:09,561 --> 00:53:13,566
Certified, but I'm not a psychiatrist.
I can't prescribe anything to you.

455
00:53:13,649 --> 00:53:17,529
I can talk to you,
I can recommend where to send you,

456
00:53:17,611 --> 00:53:19,113
but that's it.

457
00:53:21,782 --> 00:53:26,834
Now, that said, if you
want to talk, I'll listen.

458
00:53:28,747 --> 00:53:31,421
For a lot of people, that's a good start.

459
00:53:32,668 --> 00:53:35,217
Now you said here

460
00:53:35,295 --> 00:53:39,471
that your mother was diagnosed
with paranoid schizophrenia in her 30s.

461
00:53:39,550 --> 00:53:40,972
And you're at 35.

462
00:53:42,302 --> 00:53:44,475
You wanna talk about that?

463
00:53:49,017 --> 00:53:51,816
Yeah, I don't know my mother's symptoms.

464
00:53:53,105 --> 00:53:54,607
I was just 10.

465
00:53:55,899 --> 00:53:58,652
My brother was 17. And...

466
00:54:02,406 --> 00:54:05,159
I don't know. She just left me in the car

467
00:54:06,160 --> 00:54:09,289
in the parking lot
at the grocery store one day.

468
00:54:11,165 --> 00:54:13,088
And she didn't come back.

469
00:54:17,963 --> 00:54:19,431
And then they found her a week later

470
00:54:19,506 --> 00:54:22,851
eating trash out of a dumpster
in Northern Kentucky.

471
00:54:24,052 --> 00:54:27,807
My dad had to put her
in the State Hospital in Columbus.

472
00:54:29,516 --> 00:54:32,690
And she's been in assisted
living ever since.

473
00:54:37,399 --> 00:54:38,491
Yep.

474
00:54:39,777 --> 00:54:41,495
My dad raised me.

475
00:54:43,363 --> 00:54:45,161
He died last April.

476
00:54:48,702 --> 00:54:51,171
So tell me about these dreams.

477
00:55:07,262 --> 00:55:10,436
I don't know what our
schedule will be, but...

478
00:55:11,225 --> 00:55:12,317
That's all right.

479
00:55:12,392 --> 00:55:15,862
But I really do think you should
continue with the sign language.

480
00:55:16,230 --> 00:55:19,279
And any additional therapies
that kids need for the cochlear implant.

481
00:55:19,358 --> 00:55:20,860
- Absolutely.
- Okay.

482
00:55:20,943 --> 00:55:22,695
- Good night.
- Good night.

483
00:56:55,162 --> 00:56:57,130
Is anyone seeing this?

484
00:59:14,134 --> 00:59:15,181
Hey.

485
00:59:21,308 --> 00:59:23,652
It's all right. Calm down, okay?

486
00:59:28,106 --> 00:59:30,655
- Samantha?
- Are you out of your mind?

487
00:59:47,501 --> 00:59:48,923
Not a word.

488
00:59:49,377 --> 00:59:51,926
You didn't say one word about this to me.

489
00:59:52,464 --> 00:59:53,966
Don't you think you owe me that?

490
00:59:54,049 --> 00:59:56,768
Don't you think that you might
respect me enough

491
00:59:56,843 --> 00:59:59,096
to at least consider what I'd have to say?

492
01:00:02,349 --> 01:00:04,192
I didn't want you worrying about it.

493
01:00:04,768 --> 01:00:07,988
Well, I'm worried, Curtis.
How are you paying for all that?

494
01:00:11,775 --> 01:00:14,699
I got a home improvement loan
from the bank.

495
01:00:19,491 --> 01:00:22,370
How could you do that
without talking to me?

496
01:00:24,955 --> 01:00:26,628
You know the expenses we have coming up.

497
01:00:26,706 --> 01:00:30,131
You want to waste money
on a stupid tornado shelter?

498
01:00:31,378 --> 01:00:33,472
I'm doing it... I'm doing it for us.

499
01:00:33,547 --> 01:00:35,140
I know you don't understand.

500
01:00:35,215 --> 01:00:37,684
You're right. I don't understand.

501
01:00:40,220 --> 01:00:43,895
I don't understand half the stuff
you've been doing lately.

502
01:00:45,183 --> 01:00:47,481
I don't understand you
putting Red out back.

503
01:00:47,561 --> 01:00:49,234
I don't understand

504
01:00:50,814 --> 01:00:54,364
you staying up all night
in that stupid tornado shelter.

505
01:00:55,777 --> 01:00:57,029
You don't come to bed half the time.

506
01:00:57,112 --> 01:01:01,288
You leave, you don't tell me
where you're going. Explain that to me.

507
01:01:02,075 --> 01:01:03,247
Please.

508
01:01:05,537 --> 01:01:07,460
Tell me something

509
01:01:09,332 --> 01:01:12,632
that helps me understand
why you're being like this.

510
01:01:14,588 --> 01:01:16,682
There's nothing to explain.

511
01:01:22,053 --> 01:01:24,351
I'm gonna go put Hannah to bed.

512
01:02:20,320 --> 01:02:21,367
Curtis?

513
01:02:23,281 --> 01:02:24,328
Curtis?

514
01:02:28,161 --> 01:02:30,710
Baby. Oh, my God. Baby...

515
01:02:33,166 --> 01:02:34,839
Oh, my God. Baby.

516
01:02:39,673 --> 01:02:41,516
I need an ambulance!

517
01:02:42,342 --> 01:02:43,844
My husband's having a seizure.

518
01:02:43,927 --> 01:02:48,353
41800 Tindale Road.
Hurry up. He's bleeding!

519
01:02:52,269 --> 01:02:53,771
Okay.

520
01:03:01,778 --> 01:03:02,779
Honey?

521
01:03:08,702 --> 01:03:09,874
Honey?

522
01:03:17,544 --> 01:03:19,217
Honey? Are you okay?

523
01:03:28,388 --> 01:03:30,607
You were having a seizure.
I called an ambulance.

524
01:03:34,352 --> 01:03:37,401
No. It's fine. It's fine.
Don't send an ambulance.

525
01:03:37,480 --> 01:03:39,733
- What are you doing?
- It's fine.

526
01:03:45,405 --> 01:03:46,452
<i>Ma, am?</i>

527
01:03:46,531 --> 01:03:48,374
Baby, what's going on?

528
01:04:01,379 --> 01:04:03,802
I'm sorry you fellows had to come
all the way out.

529
01:04:03,882 --> 01:04:05,384
It's what we do.

530
01:04:05,467 --> 01:04:06,593
Now we can still take you in

531
01:04:06,676 --> 01:04:08,428
if you want a doctor
to look at those cuts in your mouth.

532
01:04:08,511 --> 01:04:11,435
Yeah, that's all right.
I'll see somebody on Monday.

533
01:04:11,514 --> 01:04:12,811
All right.

534
01:04:13,475 --> 01:04:14,772
Thanks.

535
01:05:01,606 --> 01:05:04,655
I haven't been honest with you.

536
01:05:07,278 --> 01:05:08,575
I'm sorry.

537
01:05:11,991 --> 01:05:13,584
What's going on?

538
01:05:18,832 --> 01:05:21,130
I've been having these dreams.

539
01:05:24,879 --> 01:05:27,632
I guess they're more like nightmares.

540
01:05:29,342 --> 01:05:31,845
It's why I've been acting like this.

541
01:05:34,347 --> 01:05:35,519
They...

542
01:05:38,143 --> 01:05:40,771
They always start with a kind of storm.

543
01:05:42,939 --> 01:05:46,694
Like a real powerful storm.

544
01:05:47,152 --> 01:05:48,870
And there's always

545
01:05:50,780 --> 01:05:52,578
this dark, thick rain.

546
01:05:52,824 --> 01:05:55,247
Like fresh motor oil.

547
01:05:58,872 --> 01:06:02,547
And then the things,

548
01:06:03,460 --> 01:06:06,930
people, it just makes them crazy.

549
01:06:09,132 --> 01:06:11,226
They attack me. Sometimes...

550
01:06:14,304 --> 01:06:16,898
Sometimes they go after Hannah.

551
01:06:19,517 --> 01:06:21,235
First one I had,

552
01:06:21,728 --> 01:06:24,197
Red nearly chewed through my arm.

553
01:06:26,357 --> 01:06:28,735
That's why you put him out back?

554
01:06:29,736 --> 01:06:30,828
Yeah.

555
01:06:39,913 --> 01:06:42,257
What was the dream? Tonight.

556
01:06:49,797 --> 01:06:51,049
It was Dewart.

557
01:06:52,509 --> 01:06:54,432
We were at the job site.

558
01:06:57,096 --> 01:06:59,849
The storm started and something happened.

559
01:07:00,058 --> 01:07:01,401
His face...

560
01:07:04,103 --> 01:07:06,231
His eyes were

561
01:07:08,858 --> 01:07:10,326
different.

562
01:07:11,361 --> 01:07:13,489
He came after me with a pickax.

563
01:07:14,656 --> 01:07:16,124
And we fought.

564
01:07:18,034 --> 01:07:20,207
And he ran it through my leg.

565
01:07:28,294 --> 01:07:31,138
It's hard to explain,

566
01:07:33,299 --> 01:07:36,599
because it's not just a dream.

567
01:07:40,640 --> 01:07:42,108
It's a feeling.

568
01:07:48,273 --> 01:07:53,404
I'm afraid something might be coming.

569
01:07:56,072 --> 01:07:57,665
Something that's

570
01:07:59,117 --> 01:08:00,494
not right.

571
01:08:04,664 --> 01:08:07,167
I cannot describe it.

572
01:08:08,209 --> 01:08:10,177
I just need you to believe me.

573
01:08:14,757 --> 01:08:16,851
I've been to a counselor.

574
01:08:19,012 --> 01:08:20,355
I've seen her...

575
01:08:21,472 --> 01:08:23,520
I've seen her a few times.

576
01:08:27,270 --> 01:08:29,443
You know what I come from.

577
01:08:33,192 --> 01:08:36,412
And I promised myself...

578
01:08:42,785 --> 01:08:46,164
I promised myself I would never leave.

579
01:08:55,089 --> 01:08:58,639
And I am doing everything that I can

580
01:09:01,262 --> 01:09:02,889
to make that true.

581
01:09:29,540 --> 01:09:31,542
Okay, since the doctor's approved
her surgery,

582
01:09:31,626 --> 01:09:34,049
we just need to get her scheduled.

583
01:09:34,128 --> 01:09:38,759
The next possible opening
is the 21st of next month.

584
01:09:38,841 --> 01:09:40,184
That's six weeks.

585
01:09:40,259 --> 01:09:42,387
- Six weeks?
- Is that okay?

586
01:09:42,720 --> 01:09:43,937
It's wonderful.

587
01:09:52,563 --> 01:09:56,033
This point just to the west.
I don't think we'll have any problem

588
01:09:56,109 --> 01:09:58,737
We should be able to get 20,
maybe 30 in this next week.

589
01:09:59,237 --> 01:10:02,116
But we're looking to see
how that's gonna shape up, so...

590
01:10:03,241 --> 01:10:04,834
- Curtis?
- Yeah.

591
01:10:05,451 --> 01:10:08,295
- What do you think?
- Yeah. That sounds good.

592
01:10:09,205 --> 01:10:10,832
We'll get it done.

593
01:10:22,343 --> 01:10:23,845
Come in.

594
01:10:26,055 --> 01:10:27,898
What you need, Curtis?

595
01:10:31,602 --> 01:10:33,980
- I need a favor, Jim.
- What's that?

596
01:10:34,063 --> 01:10:36,486
Can you take Dewart off my crew?

597
01:10:36,566 --> 01:10:38,989
Just reassign him someplace else.

598
01:10:43,656 --> 01:10:46,830
What's the trouble?
He not pulling his weight?

599
01:10:47,785 --> 01:10:50,004
No, nothing like that. He's a good worker.

600
01:10:50,079 --> 01:10:52,207
He's a good man. He's my friend.

601
01:10:54,167 --> 01:10:58,673
I think it'd be easier not being in
charge of someone I'm so close to.

602
01:10:59,505 --> 01:11:01,803
You know, I understand.

603
01:11:03,509 --> 01:11:06,934
This is part of what it means
to manage people, Curtis.

604
01:11:07,013 --> 01:11:08,435
You're gonna have to learn that.

605
01:11:09,307 --> 01:11:11,776
Yes, sir. I appreciate that, but...

606
01:11:12,769 --> 01:11:16,148
Well, it would just be
very helpful in this case.

607
01:11:17,315 --> 01:11:18,362
Okay.

608
01:11:19,609 --> 01:11:21,907
Well, I can put him with Russell.

609
01:11:21,986 --> 01:11:25,707
- Anybody else you'd prefer?
- No. Whoever you think's right.

610
01:11:27,116 --> 01:11:28,993
Okay. Okay.

611
01:11:30,077 --> 01:11:31,374
Thank you.

612
01:11:32,538 --> 01:11:35,337
You been missing a lot of work, Curtis.

613
01:11:36,083 --> 01:11:39,132
I know.
My daughter's had a lot of doctor's visits.

614
01:11:39,212 --> 01:11:40,384
I haven't let anything get behind.

615
01:11:40,630 --> 01:11:42,553
No. But don't. Okay?

616
01:11:43,299 --> 01:11:44,551
Yes, sir.

617
01:11:58,356 --> 01:12:01,109
I know they just usually
do oysters and fries,

618
01:12:01,192 --> 01:12:04,116
but what if we did
something healthier on the side?

619
01:12:05,696 --> 01:12:06,913
What, like 'slaw?

620
01:12:07,448 --> 01:12:10,247
I don't know. Maybe a vegetable or salad.

621
01:12:19,085 --> 01:12:22,635
Dewart's been telling me
how strange Curtis has been acting lately.

622
01:12:24,257 --> 01:12:25,804
I am so sorry.

623
01:12:28,010 --> 01:12:31,184
It's not like you don't have
enough on your plate with Hannah.

624
01:12:31,264 --> 01:12:32,686
Things are fine.

625
01:12:37,603 --> 01:12:39,025
We're fine.

626
01:12:52,368 --> 01:12:53,961
Can I help you?

627
01:12:54,662 --> 01:12:55,959
Yeah.

628
01:12:58,457 --> 01:13:01,301
- Can I look at one of these gas masks?
- Sure.

629
01:13:01,669 --> 01:13:02,795
Which one you want to look at?

630
01:13:03,129 --> 01:13:04,631
The newest one.

631
01:13:11,220 --> 01:13:12,972
- How much?
- $178.

632
01:13:14,265 --> 01:13:15,312
Anything cheaper?

633
01:13:15,975 --> 01:13:18,694
No. That's the cheapest
one I got in the store.

634
01:13:18,978 --> 01:13:21,527
They go all the way up to $290.

635
01:13:22,773 --> 01:13:25,322
I don't know what you want to spend,

636
01:13:25,401 --> 01:13:27,779
but a gas mask ain't something
you want to go cheap on.

637
01:13:29,405 --> 01:13:30,998
You got any kids' sizes?

638
01:13:31,407 --> 01:13:32,499
No.

639
01:13:33,075 --> 01:13:34,702
Kids can't wear those.

640
01:13:34,785 --> 01:13:37,504
They gotta have a special thing,
it's like a hood.

641
01:13:38,664 --> 01:13:40,416
I don't fool with those.

642
01:14:03,439 --> 01:14:05,533
What the hell are you doing?

643
01:14:17,536 --> 01:14:19,504
What you got going on here?

644
01:14:21,332 --> 01:14:25,883
I'm just adding on to the storm shelter.

645
01:14:27,421 --> 01:14:29,344
- Why?
- Just because.

646
01:14:32,426 --> 01:14:33,678
You running water to it?

647
01:14:33,761 --> 01:14:35,889
Yeah. From our well.

648
01:14:36,681 --> 01:14:38,979
Running sewer out to the city line.

649
01:14:40,142 --> 01:14:42,565
How much you spending on this thing?

650
01:14:42,645 --> 01:14:44,898
- It's not bad.
- Doesn't look it.

651
01:14:48,776 --> 01:14:50,824
You take your eye off the ball
one minute in this economy

652
01:14:50,903 --> 01:14:52,576
and you're screwed.

653
01:14:53,447 --> 01:14:55,745
- You got the cash for this?
- Yeah.

654
01:14:58,202 --> 01:15:00,330
Don't put nothing on credit cards.
That shit'll eat you up.

655
01:15:00,413 --> 01:15:01,585
I'm not.

656
01:15:10,297 --> 01:15:11,970
Samantha called me.

657
01:15:13,426 --> 01:15:14,678
I figured.

658
01:15:17,346 --> 01:15:19,189
Called you to come tell me to quit?

659
01:15:19,265 --> 01:15:21,267
She called 'cause she's worried.

660
01:15:21,350 --> 01:15:23,523
Says you've been stressed out.

661
01:15:26,856 --> 01:15:28,449
- So?
- So what?

662
01:15:29,233 --> 01:15:30,860
You stressed out?

663
01:15:32,862 --> 01:15:35,331
No. No more than anybody else.

664
01:15:36,949 --> 01:15:38,542
Work all right?

665
01:15:43,789 --> 01:15:46,542
Hey, look. You wanna come by and
have dinner sometime, Kyle? That's fine.

666
01:15:46,625 --> 01:15:48,502
We'll have a beer and
talk about the old days,

667
01:15:48,586 --> 01:15:49,587
but you got something to say, just say it.

668
01:15:49,670 --> 01:15:51,297
You can stop that shit right now.

669
01:15:51,380 --> 01:15:55,430
I'll come over there and remind you
what it's like to get your ass whipped.

670
01:15:59,138 --> 01:16:00,640
I'm just coming here to check on you.

671
01:16:00,723 --> 01:16:02,817
Well, I appreciate it, Kyle.

672
01:16:11,317 --> 01:16:13,160
You been to see Mom?

673
01:16:13,694 --> 01:16:15,537
Yeah. A few days ago.

674
01:16:18,324 --> 01:16:19,917
She all right?

675
01:16:22,078 --> 01:16:23,295
You should see her.

676
01:16:23,871 --> 01:16:25,589
Take your girls.

677
01:16:26,791 --> 01:16:28,839
Yeah. Yeah, I'll get around to it.

678
01:16:37,968 --> 01:16:40,391
- You need a hand?
- No. I've got it.

679
01:16:43,057 --> 01:16:44,183
Okay.

680
01:16:46,477 --> 01:16:49,230
- Call me if you need me, okay?
- I will.

681
01:16:52,024 --> 01:16:53,571
Hey, Kyle?

682
01:16:55,611 --> 01:16:58,034
Actually, you could do me a favor.

683
01:16:58,239 --> 01:17:01,083
- What's that?
- You still looking for a dog?

684
01:17:02,159 --> 01:17:03,285
Sure.

685
01:17:04,078 --> 01:17:06,706
They got a good spot for you, okay, buddy?

686
01:17:10,334 --> 01:17:12,052
- You sure?
- Yeah.

687
01:17:14,713 --> 01:17:17,182
I know it'll make my girls happy.

688
01:17:18,008 --> 01:17:19,260
All right.

689
01:17:21,720 --> 01:17:24,098
- Hey, Kyle?
- Yeah?

690
01:17:31,147 --> 01:17:32,239
Okay.

691
01:17:33,107 --> 01:17:34,905
Take care of yourself.

692
01:17:35,442 --> 01:17:38,070
All right. All right.
I will, little brother.

693
01:17:39,363 --> 01:17:42,913
You take care of your family.
Handle your business. Okay?

694
01:18:08,350 --> 01:18:09,772
All right. Bedtime.

695
01:20:20,899 --> 01:20:21,946
You okay?

696
01:20:45,174 --> 01:20:46,426
Who's that?

697
01:20:50,929 --> 01:20:52,181
Shit.

698
01:20:59,104 --> 01:21:00,105
Hey, Jim.

699
01:21:02,649 --> 01:21:03,741
Curtis.

700
01:21:08,947 --> 01:21:13,327
Dewart told me you took equipment
from work for a project at your house.

701
01:21:13,577 --> 01:21:16,581
Said that's why
you wanted him off your crew.

702
01:21:18,123 --> 01:21:20,467
I came out here to see it myself.

703
01:21:22,252 --> 01:21:25,005
Yeah. It was just a hauler and a backhoe.

704
01:21:27,341 --> 01:21:30,595
It was Saturday.
I had them back in less than eight hours.

705
01:21:30,677 --> 01:21:32,679
You know that doesn't matter.

706
01:21:36,266 --> 01:21:39,361
I can't even tell you
how many rules you broke.

707
01:21:40,104 --> 01:21:42,072
What if you had an accident? Huh?

708
01:21:42,523 --> 01:21:45,823
What if you ran somebody over
on your way out here?

709
01:21:48,112 --> 01:21:49,989
Lawsuit like that could bankrupt me.

710
01:21:50,072 --> 01:21:51,164
Well,

711
01:21:53,283 --> 01:21:54,705
I'm sorry, Jim. I hadn't thought of that.

712
01:21:54,785 --> 01:21:57,584
Thank God nothing like that happened,
you know?

713
01:21:58,747 --> 01:22:01,341
I'll do whatever I can to make it right.

714
01:22:02,000 --> 01:22:04,469
You can pick up your last check on Friday.

715
01:22:05,504 --> 01:22:07,506
You've got two weeks' benefits.

716
01:22:16,640 --> 01:22:18,642
Did you fire Dewart, too?

717
01:22:19,059 --> 01:22:21,482
He's on two weeks leave, unpaid.

718
01:22:27,776 --> 01:22:29,494
I'm sorry, Curtis.

719
01:22:32,865 --> 01:22:34,867
You did this to yourself.

720
01:22:43,333 --> 01:22:44,380
Damn.

721
01:22:59,766 --> 01:23:01,439
I've been fired.

722
01:23:06,273 --> 01:23:08,401
What about the health insurance?

723
01:23:11,528 --> 01:23:13,405
We get two more weeks.

724
01:23:22,414 --> 01:23:23,916
I'm sorry.

725
01:23:48,398 --> 01:23:50,617
- Excuse me.
- Are you Curtis?

726
01:23:51,109 --> 01:23:52,656
- Yeah.
- Come in.

727
01:23:53,278 --> 01:23:56,498
Kendra transferred out.
I'll be meeting with you today.

728
01:23:56,990 --> 01:23:58,663
Please, sit down.

729
01:24:10,963 --> 01:24:12,715
What happened to Kendra?

730
01:24:13,924 --> 01:24:18,646
She got into a program at OSU,
so she'll be transferring near there.

731
01:24:19,972 --> 01:24:22,976
I've split her caseload
with another counselor.

732
01:24:23,892 --> 01:24:26,566
It's been kind of crazy around here lately.

733
01:24:28,480 --> 01:24:29,697
So,

734
01:24:31,733 --> 01:24:33,656
I've looked over your file.

735
01:24:34,236 --> 01:24:38,207
It says your mother was diagnosed
with paranoid schizophrenia

736
01:24:38,323 --> 01:24:39,996
in her early 30s.

737
01:24:43,537 --> 01:24:45,289
Let's start there.

738
01:25:40,344 --> 01:25:42,813
I'm so sorry. I completely forgot.

739
01:25:42,888 --> 01:25:44,936
That's okay. Don't worry about it.

740
01:25:45,891 --> 01:25:48,440
- Thanks.
- Here. I hope you like them.

741
01:25:48,935 --> 01:25:51,609
- I brought cash.
- That's terrific. It's fine.

742
01:25:51,688 --> 01:25:53,782
Call me if they don't work
and I'm sorry again.

743
01:25:53,857 --> 01:25:55,859
It's okay. Thank you.

744
01:26:48,954 --> 01:26:51,457
Okay. All done. Done.

745
01:26:59,047 --> 01:27:00,469
Sweet dreams.

746
01:27:24,197 --> 01:27:25,414
What's that?

747
01:27:28,243 --> 01:27:30,621
That's the alternator from the truck.

748
01:27:33,707 --> 01:27:36,711
I was just trying to figure out a way
to charge enough batteries

749
01:27:36,793 --> 01:27:38,670
to run lights down there.

750
01:27:41,089 --> 01:27:44,559
Yeah, what the hell.
Maybe I'll hook it up to your old Exercycle.

751
01:27:51,391 --> 01:27:53,143
You gonna leave me?

752
01:27:55,771 --> 01:27:58,775
You flinched
when I touched your hand this morning.

753
01:27:59,816 --> 01:28:01,068
I'm sorry.

754
01:28:03,570 --> 01:28:05,322
I was in one of your dreams?

755
01:28:06,114 --> 01:28:07,161
Yeah.

756
01:28:10,368 --> 01:28:12,120
Can you deal with that?

757
01:28:31,056 --> 01:28:32,182
Yeah.

758
01:28:39,439 --> 01:28:41,567
Okay. Then I made a decision.

759
01:28:42,025 --> 01:28:43,652
We cancel the beach trip.

760
01:28:43,819 --> 01:28:47,790
We have enough to cover bills for
the next two months with your last check.

761
01:28:47,864 --> 01:28:51,164
I'm going to get a job.
You're gonna find another job.

762
01:28:51,243 --> 01:28:53,746
I'm going to call to see
if we can move Hannah's surgery up.

763
01:28:53,829 --> 01:28:57,504
We'll need to see what it costs to
extend your policy to the end of the year.

764
01:28:58,583 --> 01:29:00,927
I want you to see a psychiatrist.

765
01:29:02,087 --> 01:29:05,261
Not a counselor from the free clinic.
Someone good.

766
01:29:07,759 --> 01:29:10,979
Dr. Shannan gave me
the number of somebody,

767
01:29:12,138 --> 01:29:14,687
but I just don't think we can afford it.

768
01:29:16,017 --> 01:29:17,985
We'll find the money.

769
01:29:19,813 --> 01:29:22,987
Also, the Lions Club supper's this weekend.
I want you to come with me.

770
01:29:23,066 --> 01:29:24,864
I don't want to see any of those people.

771
01:29:24,943 --> 01:29:26,570
I want you to go.

772
01:29:28,446 --> 01:29:30,619
I need to do something normal.

773
01:29:41,084 --> 01:29:42,256
All right.

774
01:30:18,288 --> 01:30:21,167
- How many pieces does Hannah get?
- Just one.

775
01:31:18,098 --> 01:31:19,441
What're you doing here?

776
01:31:23,144 --> 01:31:24,737
Not here, man.

777
01:31:26,481 --> 01:31:28,483
I said, what are you doing here?

778
01:31:32,070 --> 01:31:33,071
Curtis?

779
01:31:33,989 --> 01:31:35,206
I've told people what you've been doing.

780
01:31:36,032 --> 01:31:37,204
I know.

781
01:31:38,493 --> 01:31:39,745
You cut me loose.

782
01:31:40,245 --> 01:31:41,292
Everything we been through.

783
01:31:41,538 --> 01:31:42,585
I know. I'm sorry.

784
01:31:43,790 --> 01:31:45,212
- Hey, hey.
- You ain't fucking sorry.

785
01:31:45,291 --> 01:31:46,918
- All right.
- You ain't fucking sorry.

786
01:31:47,794 --> 01:31:49,262
You sorry, you wouldn't cut me loose.

787
01:31:49,421 --> 01:31:50,968
We're fucking friends!
This how you treat friends?

788
01:31:51,047 --> 01:31:52,094
Come on.

789
01:31:53,049 --> 01:31:54,096
God damn it.

790
01:31:56,011 --> 01:31:57,058
Stop it, Dewart!

791
01:31:58,179 --> 01:31:59,226
Fuck!

792
01:32:00,974 --> 01:32:01,975
I said not here!

793
01:32:04,144 --> 01:32:05,396
God damn it!

794
01:32:09,065 --> 01:32:10,863
You think I'm crazy?

795
01:32:11,317 --> 01:32:13,160
Is that what he told you?

796
01:32:15,280 --> 01:32:17,783
Well, listen up!

797
01:32:21,786 --> 01:32:23,788
There is a storm coming

798
01:32:26,708 --> 01:32:29,131
like nothing you have ever seen!

799
01:32:29,961 --> 01:32:34,387
And not a one of you is prepared for it!

800
01:32:42,557 --> 01:32:44,400
You think I'm crazy?

801
01:32:45,226 --> 01:32:47,320
Hey, I'm talking to you, Russell!

802
01:32:48,480 --> 01:32:50,608
Lewis! You think I'm a thief?

803
01:33:04,496 --> 01:33:06,419
Sleep well in your beds.

804
01:33:06,706 --> 01:33:08,925
Because if this thing comes true,

805
01:33:11,169 --> 01:33:13,171
there ain't gonna be any more.

806
01:34:46,055 --> 01:34:47,272
Hannah?

807
01:34:50,643 --> 01:34:51,735
Hannah!

808
01:35:55,333 --> 01:35:57,256
Curtis? Wake up! Wake up!

809
01:36:55,560 --> 01:36:57,312
Come on. It's okay.

810
01:37:06,070 --> 01:37:07,447
It's okay.

811
01:37:08,740 --> 01:37:09,741
See?

812
01:37:10,742 --> 01:37:12,744
All right. Come on. Sit down.

813
01:37:13,453 --> 01:37:14,705
All right.

814
01:37:20,752 --> 01:37:22,470
Okay, honey, here you go.

815
01:37:22,545 --> 01:37:25,094
- No. Don't do that.
- It's okay. It's oxygen.

816
01:37:25,173 --> 01:37:26,891
Here. Put this on.

817
01:37:28,259 --> 01:37:30,478
- Are you kidding?
- Please, just do it.

818
01:37:30,928 --> 01:37:32,180
Okay?

819
01:37:33,139 --> 01:37:34,391
There we go.

820
01:37:36,059 --> 01:37:37,402
All right.

821
01:37:38,019 --> 01:37:40,272
Keep it out of your eyes. Okay?

822
01:37:40,480 --> 01:37:44,280
Hey. I love you. It's okay.

823
01:37:45,109 --> 01:37:47,612
All right? All right. Okay.

824
01:40:09,504 --> 01:40:11,006
Wake up, babe.

825
01:40:20,139 --> 01:40:21,265
Where's your mask?

826
01:40:21,766 --> 01:40:23,313
We took them off. It's fine.

827
01:40:23,559 --> 01:40:24,606
- No.
- Take it off.

828
01:40:25,436 --> 01:40:26,653
- No.
- Take it off.

829
01:40:27,688 --> 01:40:28,814
No.

830
01:40:29,190 --> 01:40:30,282
We're fine.

831
01:40:32,360 --> 01:40:33,407
Take it off.

832
01:41:02,306 --> 01:41:04,525
You need to open the door now.

833
01:41:10,356 --> 01:41:11,903
What if it's...

834
01:41:11,983 --> 01:41:13,326
What if it's not over?

835
01:41:15,486 --> 01:41:16,487
What?

836
01:41:20,533 --> 01:41:22,410
What if it's not over?

837
01:41:26,080 --> 01:41:27,423
It's over.

838
01:41:28,749 --> 01:41:30,217
Get the keys.

839
01:41:31,502 --> 01:41:33,004
Open the door.

840
01:43:28,369 --> 01:43:30,121
It's still storming.

841
01:43:31,706 --> 01:43:33,083
No. It's not.

842
01:43:36,085 --> 01:43:37,632
I can hear it.

843
01:43:39,630 --> 01:43:41,553
I don't hear anything.

844
01:43:48,681 --> 01:43:51,935
Put your hand on the door. You can feel it.

845
01:44:33,309 --> 01:44:35,607
Thunder? Do you feel it?

846
01:44:41,192 --> 01:44:42,318
You feel it?

847
01:44:43,027 --> 01:44:44,028
You feel it?

848
01:45:09,512 --> 01:45:10,980
I'm sorry.

849
01:45:16,143 --> 01:45:18,566
Baby, there's no storm outside.

850
01:45:26,904 --> 01:45:28,326
I'm sorry.

851
01:45:31,075 --> 01:45:33,248
Curtis, I wouldn't lie to you.

852
01:45:36,413 --> 01:45:38,211
We love you very much.

853
01:45:43,003 --> 01:45:44,596
Please

854
01:45:47,925 --> 01:45:49,427
open the door.

855
01:45:52,930 --> 01:45:54,227
I'm sorry.

856
01:45:58,143 --> 01:45:59,440
I can't.

857
01:46:19,123 --> 01:46:23,219
I love you, but if I open the door,
then nothing's gonna change.

858
01:46:24,962 --> 01:46:26,760
You'll see that everything's fine,

859
01:46:27,298 --> 01:46:29,300
but nothing will change.

860
01:46:31,176 --> 01:46:32,428
Please.

861
01:46:34,847 --> 01:46:37,521
This is what it means to stay with us.

862
01:46:45,608 --> 01:46:48,077
This is something you have to do.

863
01:47:56,762 --> 01:47:58,890
Could you move Hannah back?

864
01:50:15,901 --> 01:50:17,198
It's fine.

865
01:51:00,320 --> 01:51:03,574
Do you have any vacation time
that you can use?

866
01:51:06,493 --> 01:51:08,712
I don't have a job right now.

867
01:51:11,415 --> 01:51:13,258
Well, I know that times are hard,

868
01:51:14,710 --> 01:51:16,963
but I think it's really important
for you to separate yourself

869
01:51:17,045 --> 01:51:18,638
from that storm shelter.

870
01:51:19,840 --> 01:51:21,763
I think you need to break away
from it for a while.

871
01:51:21,842 --> 01:51:24,061
We can start you on some medication
that I think will help,

872
01:51:24,136 --> 01:51:26,810
but that action alone would mean a lot.

873
01:51:26,889 --> 01:51:30,268
We usually go on a trip
to Myrtle Beach each summer.

874
01:51:31,685 --> 01:51:33,562
We were gonna go this month.

875
01:51:34,688 --> 01:51:36,782
I think that would be okay

876
01:51:37,316 --> 01:51:39,944
if we start the medication now.

877
01:51:41,236 --> 01:51:43,330
And it would give you all some time
to prepare as a family.

878
01:51:43,405 --> 01:51:45,499
But I want to be clear,

879
01:51:45,574 --> 01:51:48,293
when Curtis gets back,
he'll need to take more time than that.

880
01:51:49,328 --> 01:51:50,955
What does that mean?

881
01:51:52,372 --> 01:51:56,172
I mean that he'll need
hands-on therapy at a real facility.

882
01:52:01,340 --> 01:52:03,843
You mean I have to leave my family?

883
01:52:08,472 --> 01:52:11,817
I think you need to
seriously commit to some treatment.

884
01:52:44,132 --> 01:52:45,179
Hey...

885
01:52:47,511 --> 01:52:48,603
Good, huh?

886
01:53:15,038 --> 01:53:16,085
Okay.

887
01:53:23,755 --> 01:53:24,972
There we go.

888
01:53:26,133 --> 01:53:27,305
Let's make a river.

889
01:53:34,558 --> 01:53:36,435
Good. Yeah.

890
01:53:39,313 --> 01:53:41,111
We put a top on it.

891
01:53:47,988 --> 01:53:49,035
What is it, honey?

892
01:53:54,995 --> 01:53:56,087
What?

893
01:55:41,893 --> 01:55:42,940
Sam.

894
01:55:47,399 --> 01:55:48,696
Okay.
